fix(touch): keep a dead SE dead, and gate TOUCHPING on a successful init

Two guards in 0120 were weaker than they read:

  - TOUCHSE cleared kt.se_dead, so re-running it after a failed recovery
    would hand the same stuck sequencer a fresh set of commands and make the
    next log unattributable.  A dead SE is now only cleared by a reboot.
  - TOUCHPING accepted kt.se != 0, but TOUCH? also maps the SE, so a probe
    alone satisfied the precondition.  Add an explicit se_initialized flag,
    set only when kt_se_init() returns true (from TOUCHSE and TOUCHINIT), and
    use it for both TOUCHPING and the state line TOUCH? now prints.

No register behaviour changes; this only tightens when a command may run.

